{"type":"text","timestamp":1785501689218,"sessionID":"ses_047d19765ffe9HfqEyjJrOZc6x","part":{"id":"prt_fb8319b9b001l218WVvZEy1bJi","messageID":"msg_fb83192f1001QZhEHlgm5znwBt","sessionID":"ses_047d19765ffe9HfqEyjJrOZc6x","type":"text","text":"Implemented core functionality to move the prototype toward a usable MVP:\n\n### Frontend (`frontend/src/App.tsx`)\n* **Added vehicle entry form** with VIN, make, model, year, and status fields.\n* Implemented `handleAddVehicle` to POST new vehicles to `/api/inventory`, update UI optimistically, and reset the form.\n* Integrated the form into the component layout before the chart.\n* Added the handler declaration after the WebSocket `useEffect`.\n\n### Backend (`backend/src/index.ts`)\n* Added **Connector endpoint** (`POST /api/connector`) that:\n  * Validates incoming vehicle data.\n  * Logs a simulated DMS push.\n  * Persists the vehicle to the in‑memory inventory.\n  * Broadcasts the addition via the existing WebSocket server.\n  * Returns a `202 Accepted` response indicating the vehicle is queued for DMS import.\n\nThese changes give salespeople a quick manual VIN entry UI (addressing the manual‑typing pain point) and lay groundwork for the connector service that will eventually push data to the dealer’s DMS. The real‑time WebSocket updates continue to keep the analytics dashboard in sync.","time":{"start":1785501686684,"end":1785501689213}}}
